In article <53795@microsoft.UUCP> gregj@microsoft.UUCP (Greg JONES) writes:
>
>Something I've run across twice (pl6) regarding loadstones:  Ran across
>a gray stone somewhere.  Picked it up.  Tried to put it down, found out
>it was cursed.  Hadn't prayed ever (and it had been a fairly long game),
>so tried praying.  Gave some friendly message, and inventory showed "an
>uncursed gray stone".  Dropped the thing, ':' said "You see here an
>uncursed gray stone".  For whatever reason, picked it up again.  Inventory
>showed "a cursed gray stone".  Arrrggggggghhh.
>
>Bug or feature?  Seems somewhat inconsistent that there is one item for
>which remove-curse isn't permanent...
>
Well, you see...

That's the point to a loadstone.  You can't drop it without it costing
you something.

In other words, if you have it, the only way to get rid of it is to
remove the curse.  EACH and EVERY time you pick it up.

Yep, it's a feature, not a bug.

-Chris
